the fixed expense ratio, though they still bear the fund's own trading costs and any excluded expenses.\n\n**If the sponsor fails to pay:** The fund remains liable. Service providers such as custodians, auditors, transfer agents, and administrators contract with the trust, so they can look to fund assets. Those amounts reduce NAV and are borne by shareholders, who can then pursue the sponsor under the agreement. The trust's board would typically act to protect the fund, which may include replacing the sponsor, terminating the arrangement, or liquidating.\n\nThis reflects general structure as I understand it through my knowledge cutoff. Specific contract terms, such as expense caps, reimbursement mechanics, and waiver provisions, vary by fund and should be checked against the prospectus and the sponsor agreement.","ttft_ms":3212,"type":"result","duration_ms":5033,"uuid":"10eb60f4-59e9-473a-9308-c421fc5a2bf5","ttft_stream_ms":475,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":475,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
